  "verdict": "The literature kernel is nearly a delta (centre voxel 0.829) yet its Wiener initialisation moves the missing voxels by 5.40e-02: missing-region MAE 0.05344 -> 0.08376 (+56.73 %), PSNR 22.881 -> 18.952 dB; DC gain 0.9524. After removing that DC factor the MAE is 0.09345 (+74.87 %), so the loss is not a brightness offset but amplified lattice-frequency artefacts (measured-region std 0.0582, 4.72 % of voxels above the reference maximum)."
